WEBVTT


00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.160
Japanese skincare and Korean skincare are not the same.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:04.840
Here are the main differences.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.280
Japanese skincare is about prevention,

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.780
fewer steps and more gentle ingredients.

00:00:09.781 --> 00:00:11.301
The focus is hydration

00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:14.281
and protecting your skin barrier for long term results.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.560
Korean skincare is about treatments,

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.720
more steps and potent actives.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.940
The focus is targeting specific concerns like acne,

00:00:21.941 --> 00:00:24.761
pigmentation and aging for faster results.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.220
If you have sensitive skin,

00:00:26.221 --> 00:00:27.821
go with Japanese skincare.

00:00:27.822 --> 00:00:29.741
And if you have active skin concerns,

00:00:29.742 --> 00:00:32.321
go with Korean. Or if you want both,

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.020
go Japanese. Hydration with Korean actives.

00:00:35.021 --> 00:00:37.361
Comment routine and I'll build you yours.
